10.3 In-Depth Line-by-Line Code Review and Operational Analysis 
A rigorous technical examination of the simulation code reveals multiple deliberate architectural 
considerations: 
• Explicit Macro Constants: #define GAS_PIN A0 and #define TEMP_PIN A1 improve firmware 
maintainability and eliminate magic numbers, allowing rapid pin remapping without modifying internal 
operational logic. 
• Floating-Point Normalization: Casting the ADC integer to floating -point via (5.0 / 1023.0) guarantees 
that the compiler generates high -precision floating -point arithmetic instructions rather than truncating 
division to integer zero. 
• Boundary Safety with constrain(): Applying constrain(responseScale, 0, 100) protects against 
unexpected math anomalies or ADC overflow, ensuring values strictly obey display buffer limits. 
• Modular LCD Screen Cycling: Splitting information across three successive screens prevents display 
line overcrowding and ensures all parameters remain readable at standard classroom distances. 
Code Portability Caution: Notice that the Tinkercad code uses Adafruit_LiquidCrystal lcd(0). This library 
is specific to Tinkercad's virtual environment. In physical hardware, the PCF8574 backpack requires 
LiquidCrystal_I2C lcd(0x27, 16, 2) or lcd(0x3F, 16, 2).

